      <p>We took what we learned and built the formula we wanted to use ourselves.</p>
      <p>Here's what's in one stick of Valor Vitals Hydration:</p>
      <p><strong>800mg sodium</strong></p>
      <p><strong>300mg potassium</strong></p>
      <p><strong>75mg magnesium, from magnesium malate</strong></p>
      <p>A lot of inexpensive formulas use magnesium oxide. We chose magnesium malate.</p>
      <p>Then there's another number on our label most people probably aren't used to looking for:</p>
      <p><strong>1,200mg chloride.</strong></p>
      <p>Most people hear "chloride" and think about a swimming pool.</p>
      <p>But chloride is also an electrolyte. In fact, it's one of the major electrolytes in your body.</p>
      <p>And each stick also contains:</p>
      <p><strong>100mg vitamin C — 111% of the Daily Value.</strong></p>
      <p>Then there's the ingredient that started this whole conversation:</p>
      <p><strong>4g palatinose.</strong></p>
      <p>Four grams of slow-release carbohydrate. 25 calories.</p>
      <p>No caffeine. No stimulants. No artificial dyes. No added cane sugar.</p>

