      <h2>So Why Do Other Hydration Packets Quit on You?</h2>
      <p>Most electrolyte products were built around a workout.</p>
      <p>You mix one before you train, while you train, or afterward. You get your electrolytes. Then you move on.</p>
      <p>That's fine if that's what you need.</p>
      <p>But some days don't end after an hour.</p>
      <p>You might be working outside. You might be on your feet all day. You might have a long shift and still have things to do when you get home.</p>
      <p>That's the use case we had in mind.</p>
      <p>A zero-sugar electrolyte product gives you electrolytes without carbohydrates.</p>
      <p>A traditional sports drink gives you electrolytes with a much larger amount of faster sugar.</p>
      <p>We wanted something between those two.</p>
      <p>Enough carbohydrate to support the absorption process, but only 4 grams.</p>
      <p>And we wanted that carbohydrate to break down slowly.</p>
      <p>That's why palatinose is there.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

